{"content_hash": "sha256:1d6823403ccfcfb8c18b178d6025a075d452b2aa5e05df35d3dc4893ac67d94b", "id": "claim:9705052v1:stabilizer-coding-space-fixed-space", "kind": "definition", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:quant-ph/9705052v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:9705052v1:general-stabilizer-code"], "supersedes": null, "text": "For an n-qubit stabilizer S that is an Abelian subgroup of the n-qubit Pauli group, the coding space T is the subspace of vectors fixed by every element of S."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:33f4da7a73898c6cbf5e06c9498bbe1fac86dfe256e7bd9af5fc839007ce7133", "id": "claim:9705052v1:stabilizer-cardinality", "kind": "equation", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:quant-ph/9705052v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:9705052v1:general-stabilizer-code"], "supersedes": null, "text": "For a stabilizer code that encodes k qubits in n qubits, the stabilizer S has 2^(n-k) elements."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:171a0784182c8ff3592ee2d683f1fe27661b86dba370525e0fb0b8a575362531", "id": "claim:9705052v1:stabilizer-fixed-space-dimension", "kind": "theorem", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:quant-ph/9705052v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:9705052v1:general-stabilizer-code"], "supersedes": null, "text": "If S is an Abelian subgroup of the n-qubit Pauli group with 2^(n-k) elements and neither i times identity nor minus identity belongs to S, then its common fixed space T has complex dimension 2^k."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:19785c806f8364fba4adaca9fa9bc1601c169f0f0c256b8f0a474c72f80e4a8d", "id": "claim:9705052v1:decoding-stabilizer-one-dimensional-fixed-space", "kind": "claim", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:quant-ph/9705052v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:9705052v1:n-generator-unique-state"], "supersedes": null, "text": "In the encoded-zero preparation construction, the stabilizer generated by M_1 through M_(n-k) together with the k encoded Z operators has a one-dimensional joint +1 eigenspace."}
{"content_hash": "sha256:e3f37649b37f93387c5bf58fc801311a31626815c41ea8d644b55af3060f76bc", "id": "claim:9705052v1:unnormalized-group-sum-lands-in-coding-space", "kind": "lemma", "origin": "SOURCE_OCCURRENCE", "paper_id": "arxiv:quant-ph/9705052v1", "produced_at": "2026-08-22T00:00:00Z", "record_revision": 1, "schema": "agtxiv.scientific-claim/1.0.0", "source_anchors": ["anchor:9705052v1:encoding-group-sum-fixedness"], "supersedes": null, "text": "For the stabilizer S and any state vector psi, the unnormalized operator sum over S sends psi to a vector fixed by every element of S, hence to the coding space T."}
